WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.870
(instrumental music)

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:02.120
- Welcome back y'all I'm hanging out with

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:04.423
Tony Gonzalez and Josh Brolin! Give it up!

00:00:04.423 --> 00:00:06.177
(cheering and applause)

00:00:06.177 --> 00:00:09.336
Later this week, I turn the big four oh

00:00:09.336 --> 00:00:10.360
(Kelly makes air horn noise)

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.950
but instead of doing too
much celebrating of myself,

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.280
I wanna celebrate others

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.190
and things that are near
and dear to my heart.

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:17.900
One of those things is reading.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:18.733
Do y'all love reading?

00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:19.760
Are y'all big readers?

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:20.593
- [Tony] Love it.

00:00:20.593 --> 00:00:21.426
- [Josh] Love

00:00:21.426 --> 00:00:22.259
- I do too.

00:00:22.259 --> 00:00:23.092
The escapism alone.

00:00:23.092 --> 00:00:24.410
So you may remember I started a reading

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:25.510
initiative this year.

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:26.770
This idea is so simple, y'all.

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.140
Strangers recommend
books to other strangers.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.220
It could be someone at a coffee
shop, a park, even online.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.057
We call it Stranger Reads.

00:00:34.057 --> 00:00:35.276
(instrumental music)

00:00:35.276 --> 00:00:38.026
♪ Stranger Reads ♪

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.880
- You better sing!

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.460
80's chick, Jessie.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.580
After our first Stranger Reads segment,

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:47.200
thousands of you took to the
comments to recommend books.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.430
I was so blown away.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:50.020
I also matched two people

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:52.450
in my audience who
exchanged their favorites.

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:53.540
They're back with us now.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:54.480
So please welcome

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.127
Hailey and Kevin!

00:00:56.127 --> 00:00:59.600
(audience cheers and applause)

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:00.433
Just to recap

00:01:00.433 --> 00:01:01.410
y'all had never met each other

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:02.820
and you had never read these books, right?

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:03.653
- No.

00:01:03.653 --> 00:01:04.486
- Right.

00:01:04.486 --> 00:01:06.570
- Okay. So what do you think,
what ended up happening?

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:09.850
- Yeah, so Kevin gave me
one of his favorite books,

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:11.560
Less by Andrew Sean Greer.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.720
And I normally don't read books like this.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:17.040
I read a lot of fantasy
and female centered stories

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.480
but this is about a gay
man who travels the world

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.700
and goes on this journey
of self-discovery.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:23.870
And I was pleasantly surprised.

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:25.140
I really loved this book.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.159
I really related to the
message that not everyone

00:01:28.159 --> 00:01:31.210
not anyone in life has a set path

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:33.860
and there's always time
to discover yourself

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.870
and establish yourself.

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:36.900
And it was just so
comforting to be reassured

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.510
that I don't need to always
know what I want to do

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:41.360
in life and that I don't
need to take life so

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:42.360
seriously all the time.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.760
And I feel like I read
it at the perfect time.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.930
And Kevin just told me that
there's a sequel coming

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:49.530
out and I'm really excited
to get to read that soon, so.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:50.780
- Oh, that's awesome.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:52.447
(applause)

00:01:52.447 --> 00:01:53.530
Kevin, what about you?

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:55.070
- Yeah. So Hailey gave me

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:57.300
An Ember in the Ashes by Sabaa Tahir.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.200
It's a young adult fantasy book.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.260
Young adult, generally isn't
a genre I gravitate towards.

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:05.130
So going into this, I didn't
really know what to expect

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:09.030
but Hailey said, this book
was the first time that

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.310
she felt represented.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:13.410
And to me being gay, finding
representation and stuff

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:14.520
like that is so important.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.230
So I knew this, like
this was gonna be special

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:18.970
and I ended up loving it

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:20.390
and relating to all these characters.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:23.290
And it's like set in this
world where people are fighting

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:25.250
against oppression and
they're trying to understand

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.120
what it means to be free.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.520
And I think that's something
we can all relate to.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.300
We all have our own, like our own fights

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.090
and they're all fighting towards love

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.370
which to me is the most important thing.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:36.320
- [Kelly] The goal. Yeah.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.580
- Yeah. And so I took so many notes

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.010
while I was reading it and
then it ends on a cliff hanger.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:40.843
So I was like, well

00:02:40.843 --> 00:02:42.964
I have to figure out what
the heck happens next.

00:02:42.964 --> 00:02:43.797
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:43.797 --> 00:02:44.630
- So there's four books total.

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.040
And I just went out and bought all three

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.590
because I was like, I'm
gonna love it anyway.

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:48.490
And yeah.

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:49.358
Thank you.

00:02:49.358 --> 00:02:50.191
(applause)

00:02:50.191 --> 00:02:51.750
- What I love about Stranger Reads is

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.220
that it's not just about
reading, it's about connection

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.090
and it just so happens that the author

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:59.660
of An Ember in the Ashes caught
our episode and reached out.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:01.959
So she's actually here,
please welcome here.

00:03:01.959 --> 00:03:04.534
Please welcome Sabaa Tahir!

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:07.867
(cheering and applause)

00:03:12.517 --> 00:03:14.417
- Hi! Nice to see you!

00:03:14.417 --> 00:03:15.871
- [Sabaa] Nice to see you too!

00:03:15.871 --> 00:03:17.009
- [Kelly] This is so cool

00:03:17.009 --> 00:03:18.880
- [Sabaa] Hello, how's it going?

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.290
- [Kelly] So it's so great to meet you.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:21.170
Say hi to everyone.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:22.140
- [Sabaa] Hello.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:22.973
Hi. Nice to meet you.

00:03:22.973 --> 00:03:24.920
- I love that you caught the episode

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:27.070
and it was so probably
random for you to see it.

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:28.250
- Oh my God.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:29.537
It was crazy.

00:03:29.537 --> 00:03:33.060
I saw it and I was like, is she holding

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.927
An Ember in the Ashes?

00:03:34.927 --> 00:03:37.150
It was like seeing your
kid on TV, you know

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.580
it's just such a crazy moment.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:42.200
And I think what hit me
about it was, you know

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.600
writing is such an isolated job.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.740
You do it alone, you
eat lots of chocolate.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.810
You cry a lot into your, into your pages

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:50.060
- Same thing with writing
songs, by the way.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.780
- Yeah. So, so you know, and so to know

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:54.360
that the book is out in the world

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.580
and people are reading it,
it's such a wonderful feeling.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.818
And with what Hailey
said, especially Hailey

00:03:59.818 --> 00:04:02.850
when you said that you felt seen

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:06.047
by the book and you felt
represented by the book

00:04:06.047 --> 00:04:07.820
that is why I wrote the book.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:09.130
- [Kelly] That was the goal.

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:09.997
- That was the goal.

00:04:09.997 --> 00:04:12.310
You know, I was a little kid growing

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:13.960
up in the Mojave desert.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:17.480
I, you know, read tons of
fantasy, like, you know

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.340
700 page book in one hand,

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:20.470
chocolate bar in the other.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:21.303
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:21.303 --> 00:04:22.890
- And during that whole time

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:24.650
I didn't really see myself in books.

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:27.650
Right. Like I just, it was,
it was the eighties, right.

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:28.810
Eighties and nineties, a fantasy.

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:31.070
So it was big hair biceps.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:31.903
- Yeah.

00:04:31.903 --> 00:04:34.315
- And very Eurocentric,
you know, very, very male.

00:04:34.315 --> 00:04:38.150
And I, when I knew, when
I wrote Ember, I was like

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:40.880
I want a brown girl to be front

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.180
and center in this book on
the cover in the narrative.

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.130
Like, that's what it was all about for me.

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:47.340
- That's so cool.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:48.820
I love that it ended up like happening

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:51.685
exactly why you wrote it is
what affected an individual.

00:04:51.685 --> 00:04:52.967
(applause)

00:04:52.967 --> 00:04:56.390
Well, Hailey and Kevin
loved An Ember in the Ashes

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:58.080
and since this is Stranger Reads

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:00.060
we wanted everyone to have it.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.056
So you're all going home with a copy.

00:05:02.056 --> 00:05:03.684
(cheers)

00:05:03.684 --> 00:05:05.435
- And you have, you have a new book out

00:05:05.435 --> 00:05:07.780
and that's more autobiographical, right?

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.248
- Yes. I do have a new book out.

00:05:10.248 --> 00:05:13.780
It took me 15 years to write the new book.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:17.390
It was a book that required
like a lot of reflection and

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:19.438
and self-love 'Cause it
was more autobiographical.

00:05:19.438 --> 00:05:20.350
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:21.544
- It's called All My Rage.

00:05:21.544 --> 00:05:23.570
It takes place in the Mojave desert.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:24.940
- [Kelly] I love the title.

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:25.773
- [Sabaa] Yes.

00:05:25.773 --> 00:05:26.606
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:05:26.606 --> 00:05:28.260
- [Sabaa] Yes. If you
are a nineties rock fan,

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.740
you know where that title came from.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:30.573
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:05:30.573 --> 00:05:32.640
- So it takes place in the desert.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:37.640
It's about two kids growing
up in a place that seems to

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:39.560
kind of wanna destroy them.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:40.853
And one is Noor.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.150
She wants to leave and go to college.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:47.550
But she, she has a family member
who doesn't want her to go.

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:49.290
And the other is Salahudin,

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:51.670
and he is trying to keep afloat

00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:53.280
a business that his parents loved.

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:55.302
And so it's about these kids
and the choices they make.

00:05:55.302 --> 00:05:56.750
- That's pressure.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:59.250
- They don't have a lot of
support they're really alone.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:01.066
And I felt that as a young person.

00:06:01.066 --> 00:06:01.899
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:01.899 --> 00:06:04.740
- And so I wanted to put
that in a book and the

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:07.250
the heart of that book and
the heart of all of my work,

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:10.350
even though All My Rage is
contemporary, it's not fantasy

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:12.270
but the heart of it is hope ultimately,

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:15.560
and hope is sort of what the
characters hold onto in Ember.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:16.970
That's what gets them through four books

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:20.090
of me being an awful evil
author and torturing them.

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:21.280
- [Kelly] Yeah. (laughs)

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.430
A really good one.

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:23.263
- [Sabaa] Thank you.

00:06:23.263 --> 00:06:25.270
And it gets them through,
through All My Rage too.

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:26.315
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:26.315 --> 00:06:27.148
- Because that's what got me

00:06:27.148 --> 00:06:27.981
through most of my life, so.

00:06:27.981 --> 00:06:29.621
- [Kelly] I think it's what
gets us through life in general.

00:06:29.621 --> 00:06:30.454
Hope. Yeah.

00:06:30.454 --> 00:06:31.287
(applause)

00:06:31.287 --> 00:06:32.980
'Cause it, you know, kinda does this

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:34.780
Well, thank you so much for coming on.

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:35.810
This is really special.

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:37.460
So I'm glad that you saw the show

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:38.400
and I'm glad that this happened.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:39.235
And I'm glad y'all love the books

00:06:39.235 --> 00:06:40.568
- Thank you. Thank you guys.

